{"seq":10,"slug":"distributed-systems","title":"分布式系统","stage":"DONE","category":"cs-fundamentals","chapterCount":5,"docCount":20,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems","rating":{"composite":3.82,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.2,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.5,"verdict":"consider","uScore":3.75}},"introMarkdown":"# 分布式系统 简介\n\n分布式系统是由多台通过网络互联的计算机协同工作、对外呈现为一个统一整体的计算系统。在当今互联网时代，几乎所有大型应用都构建在分布式架构之上——从搜索引擎到社交网络，从电商平台到云计算服务。理解分布式系统的核心原理和设计模式，是构建可扩展、高可用系统的必备能力。\n\n本手册面向后端开发工程师、架构师、SRE 工程师以及所有希望深入理解分布式计算的技术从业者。无论你是初次接触分布式概念的开发者，还是在实践中遇到分布式难题的资深工程师，都能在这里找到系统且深入的参考内容。\n\n全书将涵盖以下核心主题：分布式系统基础理论（CAP 定理、BASE 理论）、一致性模型与共识算法（Paxos、Raft）、分布式存储与数据分片策略、分布式事务与最终一致性、服务发现与负载均衡、容错机制与故障恢复、分布式消息系统，以及微服务架构下的分布式实践。通过系统学习，你将具备设计和构建可靠分布式系统的理论基础和实践能力。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"fundamentals","title":"分布式基础理论","docCount":4,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/fundamentals","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cap-and-base","title":"CAP 定理与 BASE","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/fundamentals/cap-and-base"},{"seq":2,"slug":"consistency-models","title":"一致性模型","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/fundamentals/consistency-models"},{"seq":3,"slug":"clocks-and-ordering","title":"分布式时钟与排序","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/fundamentals/clocks-and-ordering"},{"seq":4,"slug":"fault-models","title":"故障模型与容错","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/fundamentals/fault-models"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"consensus-protocols","title":"一致性协议","docCount":4,"url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/consensus-protocols","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"paxos","title":"Paxos 协议","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/consensus-protocols/paxos"},{"seq":2,"slug":"raft","title":"Raft 协议","url":"/h/cs-fundamentals/distributed-systems/consensus-protocols/raft"},{"seq":3,"slug":"zab-and-zookeeper","title":"Zab 与 ZooKeeper","url":"/h/cs-fundamental